7. Key Communication Flows
Audio Flow (User → AI → User)
Browser mic → AudioContext → downsample to 24kHz → base64
  → WebSocket → FastAPI → WebSocket → Azure Voice Live → GPT-4 Realtime
  → Response audio delta → FastAPI → WebSocket → Browser AudioContext playback
Avatar Video Flow (direct WebRTC, bypasses backend)
Browser creates RTCPeerConnection → generates SDP offer
  → POST /avatar-offer → FastAPI encodes SDP as base64 JSON → sends to Azure
  → Azure returns SDP answer → FastAPI decodes → returns to browser
  → WebRTC handshake → Azure streams avatar video+audio directly to browser
Function Call Flow
GPT-4 decides to call a tool → Azure Voice Live sends function_call event
  → FastAPI receives it → executes the tool (e.g., computeAllocation)
  → Returns result → FastAPI sends function_call_output back to Azure
  → GPT-4 incorporates result into its spoken response
8. Deterministic Allocation Engine
This is the core innovation — the LLM doesn't invent percentages. Instead:
1. 3 anchor portfolios (from real US return/vol data in asset_stats.json):
- Conservative: 18% Large Cap, 4% Small Cap, 6% REITs, 10% Gold, 32% Bond, 15% Treasury, 15% Cash
- Moderate: 38/12/8/8/22/8/4
- Aggressive: 50/22/10/6/8/4/0
2. Aria's 5 risk bands are interpolations of these 3 anchors
3. Pipeline: base → goal tilt → horizon glide → floor → normalize → rollup to 3 classes → Commodities clamp ~10% → normalize to 100
4. Feasibility: Multi-goal assessment checks if ONE monthly contribution can fund ALL goals at once
